_meanings:
(Never used at the beginning of a sentence, but usually
 after the first word)
.²1 An adversative particle meaning ‘but’, ‘on the contrary’, ‘on the other
 hand’, ‘nevertheless’; {#sa sarvezAM suKAnAmanta yayO . ekaM tu sutamuKadarSanasuKaM#}
 {#na leBe#} <ls>K. 59</ls>; {#viparyaye tu piturasyAH samIpanayanamavasTitameva#}
 <ls>Ś. 5</ls> (in this sense {#tu#} is often added to {#kiM#} and {#param#}, and
 {#kiMtu#} and {#paraMtu#} are, unlike {#tu#}, always used at the beginning
 of a sentence).
.²2 And now, on oneʼs part, and; {#ekadA tu pratIhArI samupasftyAbravIt#}
 <ls>Ks. 8</ls>; {#rAjA tu tAmAryAM SrutvA'bravIt#} <ls n="Ks.">12</ls>.
.²3 As to as regards, as for; {#pravartyatAM brAhmaRAnuddiSya pAkaH .#},
 {#candroparAgaM prati tu kenApi vipralabDAsi#} <ls>Mu. 1</ls>; <ls>Māl. 8. 4</ls>.
.²4 It sometimes marks a difference ({#Beda#}) or superior quality; {#mfzwaM#}
 {#payo mfzwataraM tu dugDam#} <ls>G. M.</ls>
.²5 Sometimes it is used as an emphatic particle; {#bAlAnAM tu SuBaM vAkyaM#}
 {#grAhmam#} <ls>Rām. 7. 83. 20</ls>. {#BImastu pARqavAnAM rOdraH#} <ls>G. M.</ls>
.²6 And sometimes it is used as a mere expletive; {#nirarTakaM tu hItyAdi#}
 {#pUraREkaprayojanam#} <ls>Chandr. 2. 6</ls>.
.²7 when used as an indeclinable it means, ‘undoubtedly’; {#tuSabdaH saMSayavyAbfttyarTaH .#}
 {#na Kalu saMSayo'sti .#} <ls>ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 74</ls>.
